Reason: Both queries pick the most‑recent ride per region in 2014‑2017, but 1result.sql is strictly deterministic: its window ordering includes trip_id as a second sort key, so if two rides share the same timestamp it still returns a single, predictable row. 2result.sql lacks that tiebreaker and could return different rows on different runs when ties occur, so 1result.sql is the safer / correct choice.